  "why": "'The Trial Part 1' against 'The Trial'. Operator, 2026-09-01: \"If there's an episode with a part number and the same title without a part number, you can't be sure which part the un-numbered episode represents.\" The plain title may be part 1, part 2, or both parts combined -- so this is neither a match nor a conflict, and it must never auto-accept. The pair deliberately carries a SHARED identity Alt ID and agrees on every other field, so the alt-id bonus and the corroboration release are both in play: verdict_not_in Accept pins that they cannot carry a title that cannot identify the record. Before eidr-core 0.26.0 the one-sided part scored a full 1.000 and this pair would have auto-accepted.",
